From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:23:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg/CfrSetupMenuDxe: Link the other pages from the
 categories

[ouroBIOS: patches/edk2/0028, without the files that TianoCore's tree
does not have (tools/edk2-import.py): 6 in edk2/OuroBiosPkg]

The categories of the CFR setup menu now also lead to the setup pages of
the other drivers, after their options: the category named by the new
PcdCfrSetupMenuGeneralCategory (General) to the time and date, firmware
update, boot splash and graphical UI pages, the one named by
PcdCfrSetupMenuPasswordCategory (Security) to the Secure Boot page,
before the password of the setup menu. The System Configuration page
still lists them all.

A link is only there with its page: the category forms end with labels,
and an EndOfDxe callback fills them with links to the formsets that are
then in the HII database, which the drivers of those pages install from
their entry points. The password link, unconditional until now, follows
the same rule. The forms themselves are still built in the entry point:
the variable policies of the read-only options have to be registered
before EndOfDxe, when the variable driver locks the policy engine.

TEST=QEMU q35 (tools/qemu-setup-shots.py of ouroBIOS): General links to
the time and date, firmware update, boot splash and graphical UI pages,
Security to Secure Boot and the password; tools/qemu-smoke.py and
tools/build.sh menu at every build; the setup of the W541 since
v1.3.10-rc12.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv

---
diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
index ed0b5f8f3..574d105a4 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
@@ -177,7 +177,14 @@ gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdPciAllocateMemoryAbove4GB|FALSE|BOOLEAN|0x00000
 #  enrolled but SecureBootEnable/SecureBoot remain disabled until toggled in setup.
 gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdSecureBootDefaultEnable|FALSE|BOOLEAN|0x0000002F
 
-## Title of the category of the CFR setup menu that ends with a link to the
-#  password asked for before the setup menu opens (UserAuthenticationDxe).
-#  An empty string leaves the link out.
+## Title of the category of the CFR setup menu that ends with links to the
+#  Secure Boot page (SecureBootConfigDxe) and to the password asked for
+#  before the setup menu opens (UserAuthenticationDxe), to those of them
+#  that are there. An empty string leaves them out.
 gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdCfrSetupMenuPasswordCategory|L"Security"|VOID*|0x00000030
+
+## Title of the category of the CFR setup menu that ends with links to the
+#  pages of the time and date, the firmware update, the boot splash and the
+#  graphical UI, to those of them that are there. An empty string leaves
+#  them out.
+gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdCfrSetupMenuGeneralCategory|L"General"|VOID*|0x00000031
